=========================================================
ADAPTER DESIGN PATTERN - XML DATA TO ANALYTICS TOOL
=========================================================

Adapter is a Structural Design Pattern that converts the interface of an existing class into another 
interface expected by the client, allowing incompatible classes to work together without modifying their existing code.

XMLToJSONAdapter IS-A DataTool
XMLToJSONAdapter HAS-A XMLData

"The client expects a DataTool interface, but the existing XMLData class doesn't implement it. 
Instead of modifying the legacy XMLData class, I created an XMLToJSONAdapter that implements DataTool and internally uses XMLData. 
The adapter converts XML to JSON, allowing the client to work without any changes."

Problem:
--------
We have XML data coming from a legacy system.

Our Data Analytics Tool accepts only JSON data.

We cannot modify:
1. Existing XMLData class (legacy/third-party code)
2. The client code that works with the DataAnalyticsTool interface

So we introduce an Adapter.

The Adapter:
1. Receives XML data from the legacy system.
2. Converts the XML into JSON.
3. Provides the interface expected by the client.

The client continues to work with the DataAnalyticsTool abstraction without
knowing anything about XMLData.

---------------------------------------------------------

Class Relationships
-------------------

XMLData
(Legacy Class)
       |
       |  HAS-A
       v
XMLToJSONAdapter  -------- IS-A --------> DataAnalyticsTool
       ^
       |
       |
     Client

---------------------------------------------------------

Workflow
--------

Legacy XML Data
        ↓
XMLToJSONAdapter
        ↓
Converts XML → JSON
        ↓
Data Analytics Tool
        ↓
Client processes the data

---------------------------------------------------------

Key Point
---------

The Adapter acts as a bridge between two incompatible interfaces.

It allows existing (legacy) code to work with new code without modifying either.

=========================================================
INTERVIEW EXPLANATION
=========================================================

We have XML data coming from a legacy system, but our Data Analytics Tool
accepts only JSON data.

Since XMLData does not implement the interface expected by the client,
we create an XMLToJSONAdapter.

The adapter implements the DataAnalyticsTool interface and internally
uses XMLData to convert XML into JSON.

The client depends only on the DataAnalyticsTool abstraction and remains
completely unaware of XMLData.

=========================================================
ONE-LINE INTERVIEW ANSWER
=========================================================

The Adapter Pattern converts the interface of an existing class into another
interface expected by the client, allowing otherwise incompatible classes to
work together without modifying their existing code.


#include <iostream>
#include <string>

using namespace std;

/*
=========================================================
Legacy Class (Adaptee)
Provides XML data
=========================================================
*/
class XMLData
{
private:
    string xmlData;

public:
    XMLData(const string& data) : xmlData(data) {}

    string getXMLData() const
    {
        return xmlData;
    }
};

/*
=========================================================
Target Interface
Expected by the Client
=========================================================
*/
class DataAnalyticsTool
{
public:
    virtual void analyseData() = 0;
    virtual ~DataAnalyticsTool() = default;
};

/*
=========================================================
Adapter
Converts XML -> JSON
=========================================================
*/
class XMLToJSONAdapter : public DataAnalyticsTool
{
private:
    XMLData* xmlData;

public:
    XMLToJSONAdapter(XMLData* data)
        : xmlData(data)
    {
    }

    void analyseData() override
    {
        // Get XML from legacy system
        string xml = xmlData->getXMLData();

        cout << "Received XML : " << xml << endl;

        // Simulate XML -> JSON conversion
        string json = "{ \"name\" : \"John\" }";

        cout << "Converted XML to JSON." << endl;

        // Analytics Tool processes JSON
        cout << "Analysing JSON : " << json << endl;
    }
};

/*
=========================================================
Client
Works only with DataAnalyticsTool
=========================================================
*/
class Client
{
public:
    void processData(DataAnalyticsTool* tool)
    {
        tool->analyseData();
    }
};

int main()
{
    // Legacy XML object
    XMLData xml("<name>John</name>");

    // Adapter wraps the legacy object
    XMLToJSONAdapter adapter(&xml);

    // Client uses only the target interface
    Client client;
    client.processData(&adapter);

    return 0;
}
